WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.373
Only 35% of companies that started onboarding to the Microsoft Store ever finished.

2
00:00:06.723 --> 00:00:09.341
For individual developers, it was 90%.

3
00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:19.677
Companies paid a $99 fee before they knew if they could pass,

4
00:00:19.677 --> 00:00:21.956
and 1 in 3 stopped right there.

5
00:00:22.306 --> 00:00:25.936
Requirements surfaced late, progress was invisible,

6
00:00:25.936 --> 00:00:30.065
and about 41% failed vetting, often with no reason given.

7
00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.629
Verification was necessary.

8
00:00:33.979 --> 00:00:35.609
The uncertainty around it wasn't.

9
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.954
First, we moved onboarding into a Store-owned flow.

10
00:00:41.304 --> 00:00:43.439
That let us drop the $99 fee,

11
00:00:43.439 --> 00:00:46.383
sign companies in with Microsoft Entra,

12
00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:50.726
and explain what verification needs before anyone commits.

13
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:56.193
Then I replaced one rigid path with three ways to verify.

14
00:00:56.543 --> 00:00:58.252
Upload a business document,

15
00:00:58.252 --> 00:01:01.352
and AI pre-fills the company details for review,

16
00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:03.314
with people still in the loop.

17
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.421
And failure became a step, not an ending.

18
00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:11.496
Email and domain are checked before anything is submitted,

19
00:01:11.496 --> 00:01:14.094
status updates live with a clear reason,

20
00:01:14.094 --> 00:01:17.211
and companies fix issues without starting over.

21
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.120
After a pilot in 50 countries,

22
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.489
it rolled out to every Store market.

23
00:01:23.839 --> 00:01:27.102
Onboarding success went from 35% to 73%,

24
00:01:27.102 --> 00:01:30.936
and vetting time fell from about 15 days to 1.

25
00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:43.714
The best onboarding doesn't remove complexity from the system.

26
00:01:44.064 --> 00:01:46.546
It absorbs it, so the user doesn't have to.
